<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toyotomi clan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Toyotomi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Toyotomi clan was the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, who unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the late sixteenth century. After his death in 1598 his young heir Hideyori was eclipsed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> profile describes how the Tokugawa eliminated the Toyotomi in the sieges of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> in 1614–1615, removing the last rival to their rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toyotomi-clan.jpg" alt="Toyotomi clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: file created on Adobe Illustrator and Photoshop by: Zagyoso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goshichi_no_kiri_inverted.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
